m-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search test investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite passes now: `python3 -m unittest` runs 16 tests with no failures. That's one more than the 15 it ran before, because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't even be imported until the first fix. I didn't change any tests.\n\nI gave the `test_search` failure to a subagent to investigate, as you asked, and tracked the work in the todo list. The fixes, all in `catalog/`:\n\n- **`search.py:3`**: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, a module that doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`, which is where `normalize` is defined.\n- **`books.py:22`**: `parse_book` kept the year as text, so `age()` crashed when subtracting it from a number. It now converts the year to an integer.\n- **`factory.py`**: `sample_books()` returned two books, but the tests (and its own docstring) expect three. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The tests only check the title, so the author, year and copy count are my choice.\n- **`fees.py:14`**: the fee added the daily rate to the days late instead of multiplying. It's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. The slice is now `[-n:]`, and I added a check so `n <= 0` returns an empty list (without it, `[-0:]` would return the whole history).\n- **`members.py:4`**: the borrowing limit was 3, but the tests and the comment above it say 5. It's now 5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params